WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 3 Student Video
Unit 1, Lesson 3: Truth

1
00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.490
2,000 years ago, Jesus said, I'm one of the ways, one of the truths, and one

2
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.730
possible life. If you want to come to the mother or the father through me, that's

3
00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:14.330
cool. Go forth living according to whatever feels right to you.

4
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.650
Okay, you got me. Clearly, Jesus didn't say that.

5
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.410
In fact, he said quite the opposite.

6
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:27.030
If you look in the New Testament, you will find at least 100 verses that make it

7
00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:32.510
clear that Jesus is the only way to God, the only way to experience an eternal

8
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:37.750
relationship with the Father. Truth is vitally important because eternity

9
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:43.590
is at stake. Now philosophers use a term that seems fancy but I think you'll find

10
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:48.330
it's kind of common sense what's called the correspondence theory of truth.

11
00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.870
And all this means is you have essentially a belief this is an idea

12
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:59.870
you hold about the world but then you have the world over here this is reality

13
00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:05.750
now truth is not a belief truth is not reality truth is when your

14
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:11.530
belief matches up with reality that's what we mean by true

15
00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:17.430
have you ever noticed how much you base your entire life down the details the daily

16
00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.870
decisions on what you think is true

17
00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.560
What if somebody says it's cold outside?

18
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.720
How do you check whether that is true or whether that's false?

19
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.520
Well, you can look at a weather app and see what information it gives you.

20
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.560
Or you could actually walk outside and you could see it for yourself.

21
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.900
If it is cold outside, then your belief is true.

22
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.980
If it's not cold outside, then the belief is false.

23
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.920
We do this with historical issues such as the claim that Jesus rose from the grave

24
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.720
and we do this with scientific matters such as the claim or the belief that the

25
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.020
universe had a beginning we actually do this on all sorts of issues we hold a

26
00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.160
variety of beliefs and then we go see if the world is the way we take it to be if

27
00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:14.560
our beliefs match up it's true if our beliefs don't it's false but remember to keep

28
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.240
this in mind our beliefs don't create reality but rather our beliefs should reflect

29
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.280
reality you might be thinking wait a minute when it comes to religious claims can't

30
00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:31.200
you have your beliefs and I have mine aren't your beliefs true for you but my

31
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.980
religious beliefs true for me not too long ago my father was speaking at a

32
00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.780
leadership event for about 400 high school students and in his session my dad

33
00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.320
decided to walk out into the audience and interact with the students and he started

34
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.340
by asking a simple question to a student that was there he said do you think the

35
00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.680
Bible is true and the student jumped in he goes yes I think the Bible's true my dad

36
00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.440
said you think it's scientifically and historically accurate in everything it

37
00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.860
teaches that we properly understand the student looked back instantly said of course

38
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:07.620
you know my dad asked this simple question back he said why the student had no

39
00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.380
answer in fact my dad went around the room and not a single student had a thoughtful

40
00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.100
answer to why he or she believed that the Bible is true.

41
00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.260
Well, the session was done and my dad was walking towards the back of the auditorium

42
00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.760
and this student comes running up to my father.

43
00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.960
He goes, Josh, Josh, I know the answer.

44
00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:28.620
I know why the Bible's true. My dad said great, why is the Bible true?

45
00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.260
He looks at my father and he says the Bible is true because I believe it.

46
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:38.280
My dad said wait a minute, the Bible's true because you believe it?

47
00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.660
What about a Quran and a Muslim who believes the Quran?

48
00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:47.280
This student looked my dad right back in the eyes and he said, If a Muslim believes

49
00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.220
the Quran is true then the Quran is true for him.

50
00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:56.640
Now my dad gave back to this student a memorable and powerful response.

51
00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.920
He said here's the difference between me and you.

52
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.120
You think the Bible is true because you believe it.

53
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.760
But I believe the Bible because I think it is true.

54
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:14.680
you see nothing is true or false because we believe it our beliefs don't change

55
00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:20.260
reality but given how important truth is let's hope that our beliefs

56
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:25.940
match up with the reality we've been talking about why truth is important but let me

57
00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:31.600
share a story about my mom to help make this point really sink in so my mom has come

58
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.160
a long ways with technology but she honestly used to be afraid of anything

59
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.100
technologically speaking in fact when my mom gets up the new technology she would

60
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:45.520
read the instructions letter by letter and followed as best as she can well she got

61
00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.840
a computer up pops something that says close all windows

62
00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:56.840
well my mom decides to and I think you see where this is going get up from her

63
00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.980
chair walk around the house and close all the windows in the house

64
00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:07.740
when she told the story obviously a little bit embarrassed we realize that truth has

65
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:13.700
consequences in this case embarrassment confusion but in many cases confusing truth

66
00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.320
can lead to devastating consequences

67
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:23.800
but when we know truth we're set free so we see a computer it's created

68
00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:28.700
and designed to function a certain way when we use it according to its design then

69
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.420
we're set free we can accomplish things.

70
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.740
But when we don't know its design, like in the story with my mom, what happens?

71
00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:39.040
Confusion, frustration and sometimes significant consequences.

72
00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:45.160
I think one of the greatest lies and confusions of our age deals with the question

73
00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.780
of what is freedom. Have you ever thought in your life what is real freedom?

74
00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.860
When I ask students to define freedom typically they'll say to me freedom is when

75
00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:57.480
you can do whatever you want to do as long as nobody is telling you how to

76
00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.460
live your life. If it feels good, do it and you're free.

77
00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:06.840
Friends, that's not freedom. Living according to whatever feels good is going to

78
00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:12.840
enslave you to your passions. Real freedom is when we embrace God's

79
00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.780
design for our life which is to love him and to love other people.

80
00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:23.360
That's why Jesus said in John chapter three that if we live according to his design

81
00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:28.920
for our life that we live in truth our works will be made known to the world

82
00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:34.060
real freedom is not living according to whatever we think is right but embracing

83
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:39.420
God's design for our life real freedom is when we live in light of truth.

